{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659780",
      "title": "Best Practice: Updating State Based On Old State Correctly",
      "sourceHash": "80b2791ad7bbb9171ba4a4cc31e5cf8f58973964841cf05aebf0919b9741ed31",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "In React, and that's now really important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 6.84,
          "en": "In React, when updating your state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.84,
          "end": 10.95,
          "en": "based on the previous value of that state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.95,
          "end": 13.59,
          "en": "you should not do it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.59,
          "end": 16.68,
          "en": "Instead, when updating your state based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.68,
          "end": 19.35,
          "en": "on the previous value of that state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.35,
          "end": 23.91,
          "en": "you should pass a function to that state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.91,
          "end": 27.84,
          "en": "This is a strong recommendation by the React team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.84,
          "end": 30.54,
          "en": "It's a best practice in the React world",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.54,
          "end": 33.75,
          "en": "and it is simply something you should memorize.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.75,
          "end": 36.39,
          "en": "When updating your state based on the previous value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.39,
          "end": 39,
          "en": "of that state, you should pass a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "to that state updating function instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 45.3,
          "en": "of that new state value you wanna have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.3,
          "end": 47.76,
          "en": "Now, why do you pass a function though?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 51.81,
          "en": "Because this function which you pass here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.81,
          "end": 53.91,
          "en": "will be called by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.91,
          "end": 57.87,
          "en": "and it will automatically get the current state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.87,
          "end": 62.31,
          "en": "So the value before this state update here as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.31,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "So in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 68.22,
          "en": "we could accept a parameter that could be named editing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.22,
          "end": 71.64,
          "en": "So this is again, true or false, just like isEditing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.64,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "But this will dynamically be set and passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 78.01,
          "en": "as a value by React when it calls this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.05,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "and this function, which you pass to setIsEditing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 86.58,
          "en": "should then return the new state you wanna set.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.58,
          "end": 90.24,
          "en": "And here we can then again use this exclamation mark trick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.24,
          "end": 92.28,
          "en": "Now with that, if you save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.28,
          "end": 95.37,
          "en": "you'll see that it still works as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.37,
          "end": 97.35,
          "en": "But of course, this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.35,
          "end": 100.59,
          "en": "now looks unnecessarily complex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.59,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "What's wrong with just using this code, which also worked?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 107.67,
          "en": "Well, the problem with this code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 107.67,
          "end": 111.33,
          "en": "is that React behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.33,
          "end": 115.05,
          "en": "is, in the end, scheduling those state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 115.05,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "you're triggering with those state updating functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "like setIsEditing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 124.38,
          "en": "So this state update here is not performed instantly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 126.21,
          "en": "Instead, it's scheduled",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 126.21,
          "end": 130.02,
          "en": "by React to be performed in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 130.02,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "Now, the future will probably be in one or two milliseconds.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "So it's really fast, but it's not instant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 138.09,
          "en": "That's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.09,
          "end": 141.3,
          "en": "Now, as a React developer, it's really important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.3,
          "end": 144.63,
          "en": "to understand that React behaves that way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.63,
          "end": 146.82,
          "en": "and that behavior also explains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.82,
          "end": 150.96,
          "en": "why when you copy this state updating function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.96,
          "end": 153.32999999999998,
          "en": "and you paste it in immediately",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.32999999999998,
          "end": 156.48,
          "en": "after the first state updating function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.48,
          "end": 159.82,
          "en": "you might not get the result you might expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.77,
          "end": 163.95,
          "en": "because here you might expect that in line seven,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.95,
          "end": 168.03,
          "en": "we setIsEditing to the opposite of what it currently is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 168.03,
          "end": 172.503,
          "en": "And since it's false by default, this should set it to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 173.7,
          "end": 175.2,
          "en": "And then, of course, in line eight",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 175.2,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "since we setIsEditing to true in line seven,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 182.28,
          "en": "we might expect to set it back to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 182.28,
          "end": 185.88,
          "en": "So with this dummy code here, which I'm adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.88,
          "end": 189.69,
          "en": "for demo purposes right now, you might expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "that in the end, nothing happens because we setIsEditing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 197.34,
          "en": "to true and then immediately to false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 197.34,
          "end": 200.46,
          "en": "So clicking the button shouldn't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.46,
          "end": 202.68,
          "en": "That would be the expectation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.68,
          "end": 206.25,
          "en": "But if we save this and you go back to the website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 206.25,
          "end": 208.86,
          "en": "you'll see that that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 208.86,
          "end": 213.86,
          "en": "Instead, if I click this edit button, the input does appear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.87,
          "end": 217.07999999999998,
          "en": "and it disappears if I click save.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 217.07999999999998,
          "end": 219.21,
          "en": "So I got the same behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.21,
          "end": 222.63,
          "en": "as I had it without this second line",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.63,
          "end": 226.173,
          "en": "because without that, we can also open and close the input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 227.19,
          "end": 231.18,
          "en": "And that's exactly why you should use this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 231.18,
          "end": 233.34,
          "en": "because with this code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 236.97,
          "en": "React is scheduling these state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 236.97,
          "end": 241.23,
          "en": "and both are based on the current value of isEditing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 241.23,
          "end": 243.24,
          "en": "which initially here is false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 243.24,
          "end": 247.92,
          "en": "So both these lines here, lines seven and eight are based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 247.92,
          "end": 252.92,
          "en": "on isEditing being false because that's the value isEditing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 253.56,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "has initially when this component function gets executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 259.35,
          "en": "for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 259.35,
          "end": 261.42,
          "en": "And since this inner function, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 261.42,
          "end": 262.95,
          "en": "gets created as part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 262.95,
          "end": 265.17,
          "en": "of the component function execution,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 265.17,
          "end": 269.34,
          "en": "isEditing has that value it has initially here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 269.34,
          "end": 272.85,
          "en": "Now, calling setIsEditing with the opposite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.85,
          "end": 277.85,
          "en": "of isEditing here does schedule a state update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 277.92,
          "end": 281.90999999999997,
          "en": "that wants to setIsEditing to true but does not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 281.90999999999997,
          "end": 285.78,
          "en": "as I just mentioned, immediately change that state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 285.78,
          "end": 287.82,
          "en": "Instead, in the next line thereafter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 287.82,
          "end": 291.57,
          "en": "we still have that same old state as we had before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.57,
          "end": 292.62,
          "en": "because we're, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 292.62,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "still in the same component function execution cycle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 297.3,
          "en": "so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 297.3,
          "end": 301.11,
          "en": "So therefore, this line also does not change the state back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 305.91,
          "en": "to false, but schedules the same update to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 305.91,
          "end": 308.4,
          "en": "and then those two schedule state updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 308.4,
          "end": 311.37,
          "en": "will be executed after each other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.37,
          "end": 314.67,
          "en": "Now, things will change if we use this function form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 314.67,
          "end": 316.503,
          "en": "for updating the state instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 317.85,
          "end": 322.036,
          "en": "If we do that in both cases, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 322.036,
          "end": 324.22,
          "en": "that now if I save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 325.26,
          "end": 328.053,
          "en": "and I click this button, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.04,
          "end": 333.36,
          "en": "And that's the case now because this first scheduled update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 333.36,
          "end": 337.02,
          "en": "does now automatically get the latest state value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 337.02,
          "end": 340.40999999999997,
          "en": "for this editing state from React at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 340.40999999999997,
          "end": 344.52,
          "en": "of time where this scheduled update is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 344.52,
          "end": 347.61,
          "en": "And here since this component just rendered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 347.61,
          "end": 350.07,
          "en": "that value will be false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.07,
          "end": 353.97,
          "en": "But then the update that's scheduled thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 353.97,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "will indeed also get that latest state value at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 362.04,
          "en": "of time where this scheduled update is executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.04,
          "end": 365.73,
          "en": "And since this second scheduled update will, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 365.73,
          "end": 368.97,
          "en": "be executed after the first scheduled update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 368.97,
          "end": 371.94,
          "en": "React will pass the updated state value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 371.94,
          "end": 374.55,
          "en": "which will be true in this case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 374.55,
          "end": 378.723,
          "en": "to that function when it is being executed by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 379.62,
          "end": 382.38,
          "en": "And that's why it's considered a good practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 382.38,
          "end": 384.87,
          "en": "to use this function form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 384.87,
          "end": 386.88,
          "en": "for updating the state instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 386.88,
          "end": 389.79,
          "en": "of using this way of updating it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 389.79,
          "end": 391.92,
          "en": "because when using the function form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 391.92,
          "end": 394.83,
          "en": "you simply have a guarantee by React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 394.83,
          "end": 396.51,
          "en": "that you'll always be working",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 396.51,
          "end": 400.5,
          "en": "with the latest available state value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 400.5,
          "end": 402.54,
          "en": "So again, even though it's not needed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 402.54,
          "end": 404.37,
          "en": "this is simply a best practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 404.37,
          "end": 406.05,
          "en": "and something you should keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 406.05,
          "end": 408.65999999999997,
          "en": "if you are updating your state based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.65999999999997,
          "end": 411.15,
          "en": "on a previous state value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.15,
          "end": 413.76,
          "en": "you should use this function form here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 413.76,
          "end": 416.34000000000003,
          "en": "of the state updating function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 416.34000000000003,
          "end": 419.28,
          "en": "And with that, we can still open and close this input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 419.28,
          "end": 422.223,
          "en": "but we're now doing it in a best practice way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}